P-G2, spec 001 group 6 (W1; tasks.md T165; plan.md §14, §16 W1's departure 14): the guards for W1's two new
Author-only targets, for the Author's hand.

.claude/hooks/bash-gate.sh, redteam/forbidden-actions.sh, and tools/gates/matrix-required.txt are the enforcement
layer's and the gate's, so their change is the Author's (tasks.md Format, "Patches"). Group 6 adds two Author-only
targets that no rule names yet: the shared state's CA and server certificate (`shared-state-tls`) and its restore from
a backup (`shared-state-restore`). The roles target, `shared-state-roles`, is P-1's already. This patch:
  - adds both to the bash gate's P-1 list of Author-only targets, so every spelling the gate reads for that list
    refuses them (a path to make, gmake, -C, a wrapper, ./, quotes in or around the name, a subshell, bash -c);
  - adds thirteen matrix rows, twelve blocks in those spellings and one allow, `shared-state-tlsx`, a name the
    rule's word boundary keeps out, each in matrix-required.txt so none can be dropped quietly.
No row is a gap: on an export with this patch, each block row blocks. The design adds no environment name (tasks.md
T165's table): the CA certificate, GATEWAY_DB_TLS_CA, is public material, and the role passwords are P-1's DB_*
names. Applies to main's copies, which no other W1 patch changes.

Built from plain copies (git show HEAD:<path> into $TMPDIR), edited, then diff -u with a/ and b/ labels; never git
apply. Apply it on W1's -p branch before W1's gate (T171), with `patch -p1 < <this file>` at the repository's root.
--- a/.claude/hooks/bash-gate.sh
+++ b/.claude/hooks/bash-gate.sh
@@ -374,12 +374,13 @@
 # The Author-only targets (research.md R-16, R-32; contracts/infra-records.md §1): make plan with a ROOT (the real plan,
 # with his SSO session; make plan alone is the offline checks), infra-verify, infra-record, infra-mirror, infra-audit,
 # secrets-check, release, rollback, the ec2-* commands, cloud-session, shared-state-roles, server-budget-restore,
-# tunnel-keys, and tunnel-revoke, by make's two matches above. make aws-login, already refused, takes a named profile
+# tunnel-keys, and tunnel-revoke, by make's two matches above; and, from spec 001 group 6 (its tasks.md T165, P-G2),
+# shared-state-tls and shared-state-restore, the shared state's CA and its restore from a backup. make aws-login, already refused, takes a named profile
 # now; operator-* with ENV=shared is refused by the dev-cpu rule below. Their API equivalents too: the AWS CLI writing or
 # deleting a /h4reet/ parameter (the secrets and the autostart switch, R-26; FR-012) or invoking h4-ec2-start or
 # h4-ec2-guard (make ec2-start's function).
 p1_route="the Author runs it in his terminal (spec 001 research.md R-32); ask the Author"
-p1_targets="$(spelled infra-verify)|$(spelled infra-record)|$(spelled infra-mirror)|$(spelled infra-audit)|$(spelled secrets-check)|$(spelled release)|$(spelled rollback)|$(spelled ec2-)[[:alnum:]_\"'\\\$-]*|$(spelled cloud-session)|$(spelled shared-state-roles)|$(spelled server-budget-restore)|$(spelled tunnel-keys)|$(spelled tunnel-revoke)"
+p1_targets="$(spelled infra-verify)|$(spelled infra-record)|$(spelled infra-mirror)|$(spelled infra-audit)|$(spelled secrets-check)|$(spelled release)|$(spelled rollback)|$(spelled ec2-)[[:alnum:]_\"'\\\$-]*|$(spelled cloud-session)|$(spelled shared-state-roles)|$(spelled server-budget-restore)|$(spelled tunnel-keys)|$(spelled tunnel-revoke)|$(spelled shared-state-tls)|$(spelled shared-state-restore)"
 if has "$make_word" && has "${tb}(${p1_targets})${te}"; then
   block "an Author-only make target (spec 001)" "$p1_route"
 fi
